  "question": {
    "text": "The mass of a pendulum bob is m = 2 kg and the length of the string is&nbsp;<math><mi>l</mi></math>. It is displaced through <math><mn>90</mn><mo>°</mo></math> from the vertical and released. What minimum tension (in N) should the string should be able to withstand so that it doesn't break during motion?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "60",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Velocity at the lowest point, <math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi>l</mi></msqrt></math><br /><br />At the lowest point, the tension in the string<br /><br /><math><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi> = 60 N </mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
